         "plotFull": "<p>High and Low (Japanese: 天国と地獄, Hepburn: Tengoku to Jigoku, literally \"Heaven and Hell\") is a 1963 Japanese police procedural crime film directed by Akira Kurosawa, starring Toshiro Mifune, Tatsuya Nakadai and Kyōko Kagawa. The film is loosely based on the 1959 novel King's Ransom by Ed McBain (Evan Hunter).</p>"
