               "rate": "6",
               "title": "I could not get past the soundtrack",
               "content": "I respect the \"classic\" status of The Third Man, but I could not get past the soundtrack. The zither music was distracting to me and it ruined what could have been some intense moments. The story was slow, but interesting and the characters were awkward, but relatable. I still think Orson Welles is a bit overrated, but he was excellent in this film."
