               "title": "Groundbreaking docu-drama",
               "content": "(1966)The Battle of Algiers/ La battaglia di Algeri (In Italian, French, Arabic with English subtitles) POLITICAL DRAMA/ DOCUMENTARYNot so much of a war film as much as a film that \"states\" about actual Algerian history when the French moved into the territory creating hostility! Some of it's themes echoes what is happening in real life, such as between Palestine/ Israel, Northern Ireland/ England to name two when one ethnic group can't settle their differences with another creating extreme radicalism by using physical, perhaps unnecessary 'violence' by using terrorist acts! Like the IRA of Northern Ireland- the Arabs in Algeria also started the FLN (National Liberation Front) either to retaliate or as retribution against the French, using some actual 'news' footage's on specific parts of this film! Groundbreaking and influential because of stating history which is similar to films such as \"Sunday, Bloody, Sunday\", \"The Kite Runner\", \"Cry Freedom\" to name a few! Although, I may have been ignorant about Algerian history and very appreciative to have seen this since it's unbiased, my rating might've been much higher had it shown actual footage's about what French governments or any other had to say 'verbally' about the hostility."
