               "username": "sterlin_rivera",
               "warningSpoilers": false,
               "date": "18 December 2021",
               "rate": "",
               "title": "Plain Phenomenal",
               "content": "Heat is quite possibly the greatest crime/heist film ever made. For nearly 3 hours, it runs in an astounding pace and is loaded with entertainment.Heat is about Neil McCauley (Robert De Niro) who him and his crew are professional bank robbers. Neil plans one last heist before his retirement, and that heist goes terribly wrong, leading to homicide. The LAPD are after them, led by Lt. Vincent Hanna (Al Pacino), and Neil and his team do what they can playing a deadly cat-and-mouse game with Vincent and his crew and hopefully make a getaway.Heat is just plain phenomenal. The acting from everyone was awesome. It was great to finally have two legends, De Niro and Pacino, in the same scenes together and they worked so good in the film as well as Val Kilmer turning in an awesome performance.The shootout scenes are epic, especially the famous one that is in the middle of the movie thag is super loud but sounds insanely great. The story was also really well put together, well thought out, and it worked for a 3 hour film. The ending also is so intriguing that it keeps your eyes locked on the screen and makes you really want to see what happens.Bottom line, Heat is one of my all time favorite movies and is actually my 2nd favorite Robert De Niro film (1st being Goodfellas)."
