               "rate": "10",
               "title": "Love it. Grim, realistic, a classic.",
               "content": "This film defines an era in the UK, a grim reality on the fringes of society.It's delightful script, story telling, cast, and visuals take us back to that feeling of being in the 90s.Along with a banging sound track, and a perfect ending, Danny Boyle is possibly the greatest director to emerge from the UK.Steve Irwing adaption was great, for that I chose life and chose 10."
