               "rate": "2",
               "title": "Greatest film ever? Really?",
               "content": "Everybody exaggerates by lifting this film in glory, considering it a super masterpiece. I don't. It's just another ordinary American movie, it didn't even make me laugh, although it's kind of like Comedy. Jeff Bridges and John Goodman are the same as in all their other films and the script is as trivial and already known from many other films, nothing original, mistaken identity. Steve Buscemi is the same too, having an almost silent role here. The only more special ones are Julianne Moore and John Turturro. With their performances they don't save the film being just an average mediocre production made in the movie making factory on the treadmill also called Hollywood."
