               "rate": "10",
               "title": "An absolute cinematic gem!",
               "content": "As Clint Eastwood reaches the end of his life, he presents us with yet another performance which is nothing short of legendary. Wishing to preserve the element of surprise, I will not reveal anything by trying to analyse this great work of art. I will say this. There are similar qualities to his previous work, but I would say that both his directing and acting have reached a level of maturity comparable to that of an excellent wine. The story was compelling and, mixed with the drama was a refined touch of humour; the perfect combination for a pleasant evening. I would like to finish by thanking Mr. Eastwood for sharing this touching moment with his audience at a time when most of the cinematic \"art\" produced in Hollywood consists of stunts and bad jokes."
