               "rate": "8",
               "title": "The Conflict is Better than any Superhero Movie",
               "content": "The story of a jazz drummer who is pushed to the brink by sadistic music conductor.As a drummer myself, I found the depiction of the art, the the elements of 'the band room' very accurate - with the exception of the crazy conductor (mine was quite nice by contrast). What makes this film so excellent is the character driven storytelling. I watched this the same weekend as Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness (\"MOM\"), and I was far more captivated by the conflict between the characters of Whiplash than I was of MOM.Whiplash featured incredible twists and turns, that kept me glued to the screen. This is an underrated gem that deserves more praise."
